From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 12:13:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tapdisk: blkif: make data structures and IPC multi-queue
 aware

Extend the blkif interface to support multiple queues per device:
- Add per-queue fields (ring, port, request pool) to td_xenblkif
- Update XenStore reading to parse per-queue ring-ref and event-channel
- Change IPC message to carry arrays of grant refs and event channel
  ports, one per queue
- Thread nr_queues through control path and connect/disconnect APIs

tapdisk is multi-queue from the domU point of view but every request
(from different event-channel) share the same lists; and tapdisk
is still mono-thread.

Signed-off-by: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
